  "id": "accommodation",
  "term": "accommodation",
  "definition": "Accommodation, in this context, means changing parts of one’s speech to become more like or less like the person one is talking with. It can involve features such as speaking rate, pronunciation, or prosody, and may reflect social aims, automatic alignment processes, or both.",
